      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The majority will hold that at least one parent has Article III injury in fact because, accepting the complaint's account of Washington's statutory scheme, nonaffirming parents are objects of a state-created exclusion from decisions about their minor children's mental-health care, so the pleaded present constraint on parenting is traceable to the laws rather than a self-inflicted response to speculative future harm."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The Court will announce a rule limited to parents of minor children plausibly exposed to a law that deliberately reallocates parental authority: they need not wait until the child enters the regulated program or receives treatment, but generalized disagreement with a law or an unparticularized future chain remains insufficient."
    }
  ],
